WEBVTT

00:00:02.690 --> 00:00:04.560
The weather's nice again today,

00:00:04.560 --> 00:00:06.640
so water tastes yummy!

00:00:06.640 --> 00:00:08.410
Are you full yet?

00:00:08.410 --> 00:00:10.420
Yes, we're full!

00:00:11.240 --> 00:00:12.560
Good morning.

00:00:12.560 --> 00:00:13.320
Oh, morning.

00:00:13.920 --> 00:00:15.350
Morning, Ichijo!

00:00:15.350 --> 00:00:17.350
That's "Ichijo-san."

00:00:17.350 --> 00:00:18.930
Go put that away.

00:00:18.930 --> 00:00:19.690
Okay.

00:00:19.690 --> 00:00:22.120
Ichijo, we're gonna ride on a train!

00:00:22.440 --> 00:00:23.830
"Ichijo-san."

00:00:23.830 --> 00:00:24.920
San!

00:00:24.920 --> 00:00:26.070
I swear...

00:00:26.500 --> 00:00:28.630
<b>Harajuku Station</b>

00:00:30.090 --> 00:00:31.350
So many people!

00:00:31.350 --> 00:00:32.970
Because it's a weekend.

00:00:33.330 --> 00:00:35.130
Shall we take the subway?

00:00:35.130 --> 00:00:38.030
Nah, she'll probably want 
to see the scenery.

00:00:38.520 --> 00:00:40.510
Sana, let's buy our tickets.

00:00:43.950 --> 00:00:45.480
What's a "ticket"?

00:00:45.480 --> 00:00:47.860
You use it to ride a train.

00:00:47.860 --> 00:00:50.400
First, push where it says "child."

00:00:51.480 --> 00:00:52.610
Here?

00:00:53.270 --> 00:00:56.250
Then push the button with the 
fare to your destination.

00:00:56.700 --> 00:00:58.900
What's half of 550 yen?

00:00:58.900 --> 00:01:00.600
275 yen!

00:01:00.600 --> 00:01:03.120
Then, select 270 yen.

00:01:04.040 --> 00:01:05.200
Why?

00:01:05.890 --> 00:01:08.420
Uh, that's just how it works.

00:01:14.330 --> 00:01:17.540
You put your ticket in. 
Then take it when it pops out.

00:01:17.540 --> 00:01:18.370
Try it.

00:01:18.370 --> 00:01:19.300
O-Okay.

00:01:25.680 --> 00:01:26.600
I got it!

00:01:28.840 --> 00:01:30.140
What is that?

00:01:30.140 --> 00:01:32.230
A card that works as a ticket.

00:01:32.230 --> 00:01:34.950
No fair! I want one that beeps, too!

00:01:34.950 --> 00:01:36.610
You won't be riding often enough.

00:01:36.610 --> 00:01:38.650
I want a beep one!

00:01:45.480 --> 00:01:47.280
She's enjoying herself...

00:01:47.280 --> 00:01:49.500
It's her first long trip.

00:03:22.970 --> 00:03:27.970
<b>Friends</b>

00:03:29.100 --> 00:03:31.560
Sorry to leave the rest to you.

00:03:31.560 --> 00:03:32.620
Not at all.

00:03:32.620 --> 00:03:34.480
This is part of my job.

00:03:34.480 --> 00:03:37.590
Make sure you do as Ichijo-san says.

00:03:37.590 --> 00:03:38.280
Okay.

00:03:38.490 --> 00:03:40.820
Good luck with work, Zoroku!

00:03:40.820 --> 00:03:42.640
See you later, then.

00:03:42.640 --> 00:03:44.030
See you later.

00:03:49.650 --> 00:03:51.700
What is this?!

00:03:55.010 --> 00:03:56.710
It's called the ocean.

00:03:57.000 --> 00:03:58.060
Ocean?

00:03:58.060 --> 00:03:58.920
Yes.

00:04:02.840 --> 00:04:04.280
Something smells.

00:04:04.280 --> 00:04:06.350
That's dangerous, Sana-chan!

00:04:11.390 --> 00:04:13.480
La, la, la, singing...

00:04:14.030 --> 00:04:15.100
Done!

00:04:15.100 --> 00:04:17.440
All right, very good.

00:04:19.720 --> 00:04:21.360
You got everything correct!

00:04:21.360 --> 00:04:22.980
That's excellent, Sana-chan.

00:04:22.980 --> 00:04:23.990
Right?

00:04:24.490 --> 00:04:26.000
If you keep up the pace,

00:04:26.000 --> 00:04:29.480
you'll complete high school 
first-year math soon.

00:04:28.700 --> 00:04:34.370
<b>Factorization 
1. Factor the following equations.</b>

00:04:29.690 --> 00:04:32.580
We've already reached the limit 
of what I can teach you,

00:04:32.580 --> 00:04:34.370
so I'll have to talk to Naito.

00:04:34.750 --> 00:04:37.840
Really? But isn't math easy?

00:04:37.840 --> 00:04:39.240
Is it?

00:04:39.240 --> 00:04:42.820
I do have a teaching license 
for elementary school,

00:04:42.820 --> 00:04:44.470
but you've put me to shame.

00:04:45.630 --> 00:04:48.910
Well, in math, the methods 
and answers are all defined.

00:04:48.910 --> 00:04:51.060
Watering flowers is more, like...

00:04:51.370 --> 00:04:54.860
The conditions aren't always what 
you'd expect, so it's harder.

00:04:54.860 --> 00:04:57.560
Every day, you have to examine 
them and see their needs.

00:04:57.800 --> 00:05:00.770
What you struggle with 
is word problems...

00:05:00.770 --> 00:05:02.040
Also reading.

00:05:02.560 --> 00:05:05.500
It would help if you could 
focus a bit longer.

00:05:05.500 --> 00:05:09.430
But I hate things like that. 
They make me feel frazzled.

00:05:09.430 --> 00:05:10.780
Frazzled?

00:05:11.130 --> 00:05:13.500
I don't really understand it,

00:05:13.500 --> 00:05:15.600
but I feel it right here.

00:05:15.600 --> 00:05:17.500
I don't deal well with those things,

00:05:17.500 --> 00:05:19.400
because I don't understand them.

00:05:20.790 --> 00:05:22.290
That makes sense.

00:05:22.290 --> 00:05:24.720
You had trouble transcribing kanji, too.

00:05:24.720 --> 00:05:27.820
Next week, let's work a little 
harder on language arts.

00:05:27.820 --> 00:05:28.340
Eh?

00:05:28.340 --> 00:05:30.940
Huh? Huh?!

00:05:30.940 --> 00:05:32.560
Let's get moving.

00:05:32.560 --> 00:05:35.110
Then, social studies is up next!

00:05:35.110 --> 00:05:36.230
We're studying more?

00:05:36.230 --> 00:05:38.600
Since we're all the way in Yokohama,

00:05:38.600 --> 00:05:43.810
Naito has made arrangements for 
us to visit a nearby factory.

00:05:43.810 --> 00:05:46.560
Wow, Naito is very clever.

00:05:46.890 --> 00:05:48.640
We're visiting a car factory today.

00:05:48.640 --> 00:05:49.810
Wow!

00:05:51.230 --> 00:05:55.370
Exclusively using seasonal 
flowers is a good idea.

00:05:55.720 --> 00:05:59.790
If you want a natural look, we can 
use smaller flowers, like this.

00:06:00.210 --> 00:06:01.730
Oh, beautiful!

00:06:01.730 --> 00:06:02.590
Huh...

00:06:02.860 --> 00:06:05.880
If you'll allow me to choose 
the flowers we use,

00:06:05.880 --> 00:06:08.880
we can easily keep it 
within your budget.

00:06:08.880 --> 00:06:10.790
That sounds great.

00:06:10.790 --> 00:06:12.120
Doesn't it, Ko-kun?

00:06:12.120 --> 00:06:13.350
Sure, it's up to you.

00:06:13.350 --> 00:06:15.710
Come on... This is important.

00:06:20.730 --> 00:06:22.500
Zoroku!

00:06:24.500 --> 00:06:25.360
Whoa.

00:06:25.550 --> 00:06:27.690
Are you done with work? 
That took a while!

00:06:28.120 --> 00:06:29.490
Were you a good girl?

00:06:29.810 --> 00:06:32.320
Yeah! We went to a car factory!

00:06:32.320 --> 00:06:35.680
It was really cool! 
Everything is made by robots!

00:06:35.680 --> 00:06:37.040
Is that so?

00:06:37.040 --> 00:06:38.520
Did anything happen?

00:06:38.520 --> 00:06:40.670
No, nothing in particular.

00:06:40.670 --> 00:06:41.580
Well, good.

00:06:47.900 --> 00:06:48.880
Error...

00:06:53.800 --> 00:06:55.760
<b>Chinatown</b>

00:06:54.530 --> 00:06:55.760
This is good!

00:06:56.020 --> 00:06:58.920
Excuse me! I'll take thirty 
more of the pork buns!

00:06:58.920 --> 00:07:00.400
No, not for gifts—

00:07:00.400 --> 00:07:01.240
Uh, no, we don't...

00:07:01.240 --> 00:07:04.190
Oh, you don't have that 
many made? Then...

00:07:04.190 --> 00:07:07.140
Then give me however 
many you have!

00:07:07.140 --> 00:07:08.170
All of them!

00:07:08.170 --> 00:07:09.010
There she is.

00:07:09.010 --> 00:07:10.960
O-Onee-sama!

00:07:10.960 --> 00:07:14.130
Yonaga, you're late. 
Try not to wander away.

00:07:14.130 --> 00:07:17.200
Y-You were the one who 
just disappeared!

00:07:17.360 --> 00:07:19.460
And you bought all that...

00:07:19.460 --> 00:07:22.040
I found these great pork buns.

00:07:22.040 --> 00:07:24.130
Here, try one.

00:07:25.640 --> 00:07:29.480
O-Onee-sama, we need to be 
careful with our money...

00:07:29.480 --> 00:07:31.170
What are you talking about?

00:07:31.170 --> 00:07:34.900
We saved it, all so we could 
eat till we dropped today.

00:07:34.900 --> 00:07:37.470
We haven't nearly used it all yet!

00:07:37.470 --> 00:07:38.720
B-B-But...

00:07:39.180 --> 00:07:43.340
You're the one who said we should 
buy from many different places.

00:07:43.340 --> 00:07:45.340
We even looked them up already,

00:07:45.340 --> 00:07:49.030
but s-since you keep making stops, 
we haven't visited one!

00:07:50.240 --> 00:07:52.360
Plans are no more than plans!

00:07:52.820 --> 00:07:55.660
First, you have to enjoy it 
with all you've got!

00:07:58.240 --> 00:07:59.450
Thank you.

00:08:02.030 --> 00:08:05.120
Onee-sama, it's been a long time...

00:08:05.120 --> 00:08:08.720
s-since the two of us went 
shopping like this.

00:08:09.440 --> 00:08:13.880
I... I never thought we'd... 
get to do this again.

00:08:15.230 --> 00:08:16.330
I know!

00:08:17.470 --> 00:08:20.650
So we'll have fun today, Yonaga!

00:08:21.870 --> 00:08:23.390
O-Okay!

00:08:23.390 --> 00:08:25.260
Maps! Restaurants! Roads!

00:08:25.260 --> 00:08:25.900
Yes!

00:08:25.900 --> 00:08:28.540
O-Onee-sama, look out!

00:08:30.610 --> 00:08:31.640
Onee-sama!

00:08:31.640 --> 00:08:32.490
I'm sorr—

00:08:33.960 --> 00:08:34.820
Sa-chan?

00:08:39.440 --> 00:08:40.500
Stop!

00:08:42.270 --> 00:08:43.390
They ran!

00:08:44.100 --> 00:08:45.880
Operation 4-18.

00:08:45.880 --> 00:08:46.840
After them.

00:08:49.240 --> 00:08:51.300
Wait!

00:08:54.340 --> 00:08:55.720
What's that? A chain?

00:08:57.080 --> 00:08:58.760
No fair!

00:08:59.790 --> 00:09:01.750
Why did we run away?

00:09:01.750 --> 00:09:03.230
I don't know.

00:09:03.950 --> 00:09:05.580
But we did...

00:09:05.580 --> 00:09:06.620
Yeah.

00:09:06.620 --> 00:09:07.690
So...

00:09:08.390 --> 00:09:09.570
Let's run!

00:09:19.290 --> 00:09:20.280
I won't let you get away.

00:09:21.440 --> 00:09:21.990
Net!

00:09:25.840 --> 00:09:27.340
Darn it...

00:09:28.420 --> 00:09:29.690
Robot!

00:09:31.320 --> 00:09:34.060
Don't think you can beat me at tag.

00:09:38.340 --> 00:09:39.240
Motorcycle!

00:09:42.560 --> 00:09:43.240
What is that?

00:09:43.240 --> 00:09:44.100
A motorcycle?

00:09:44.300 --> 00:09:46.060
Wait!

00:09:46.060 --> 00:09:47.670
Why are you running away?!

00:09:47.670 --> 00:09:50.330
Why are <i>you</i> chasing us?

00:09:50.330 --> 00:09:52.990
I don't know! It just made 
me feel frazzled!

00:09:52.990 --> 00:09:54.050
What?!

00:09:54.050 --> 00:09:56.030
"It just made me feel frazzled," I said!

00:09:54.310 --> 00:09:55.650
Hey, what's that?

00:09:55.800 --> 00:09:57.780
Some kind of circus?

00:09:58.300 --> 00:09:59.350
Incredible...

00:09:59.350 --> 00:10:01.620
That's one amazing stuntman!

00:10:02.040 --> 00:10:03.580
Those kids...

00:10:03.810 --> 00:10:05.200
Why are you running away?

00:10:05.200 --> 00:10:07.490
Because we don't want 
to see you, obviously!

00:10:07.490 --> 00:10:09.230
At least figure that much out!

00:10:09.230 --> 00:10:11.250
Wh-What do you mean? Why not?

00:10:11.250 --> 00:10:13.710
You have to tell me, 
or I won't under—

00:10:18.180 --> 00:10:19.050
Sa-chan!

00:10:20.060 --> 00:10:21.110
Error.

00:10:28.380 --> 00:10:30.160
Operation 13-7.

00:10:30.160 --> 00:10:30.940
Summon beast.

00:10:32.560 --> 00:10:33.480
Fenrir.

00:10:35.490 --> 00:10:37.530
All three of you will be punished.

00:10:37.910 --> 00:10:40.440
#51, operation 1-8.

00:10:42.750 --> 00:10:45.080
Deploy operation 5-16.

00:10:45.080 --> 00:10:46.110
Fenrir.

00:10:54.320 --> 00:10:55.460
And now, 1-8.

00:10:57.170 --> 00:10:58.230
Super-accelerate!

00:11:11.940 --> 00:11:14.150
<b>Chinatown</b>

00:11:16.230 --> 00:11:17.350
Welcome.

00:11:17.350 --> 00:11:18.770
The name on your reservation?

00:11:20.280 --> 00:11:21.650
Kashimura Sana!

00:11:21.650 --> 00:11:23.620
All right, just a moment, please.

00:11:24.340 --> 00:11:25.700
Kashimura?

00:11:26.580 --> 00:11:28.070
I'm Kashimura Sana!

00:11:29.480 --> 00:11:31.060
As far as I can tell,

00:11:31.060 --> 00:11:33.210
it just appears to be a 
lump of carbon again.

00:11:33.910 --> 00:11:34.880
Yes.

00:11:34.880 --> 00:11:39.060
We managed to convince everyone 
that we were filming a movie,

00:11:39.060 --> 00:11:41.490
but take care of any 
photos on the Internet.

00:11:42.180 --> 00:11:44.720
Yes, the twins are currently...

00:11:46.010 --> 00:11:47.480
Hurry up and sit down.

00:11:47.480 --> 00:11:48.920
We're ordering.

00:11:48.920 --> 00:11:50.720
U-Um...

00:11:50.720 --> 00:11:52.950
We should really...

00:11:53.550 --> 00:11:55.990
You already apologized 
to Ichijo-san, right?

00:11:55.990 --> 00:11:57.020
So it's fine.

00:11:57.590 --> 00:11:58.680
Okay...

00:12:00.400 --> 00:12:03.190
Is there anything you two can't eat?

00:12:03.190 --> 00:12:05.270
If not, I'll just order whatever.

00:12:05.270 --> 00:12:07.440
Oh, y-yes, thank you.

00:12:07.440 --> 00:12:08.740
Y-Yonaga!

00:12:14.110 --> 00:12:15.880
Oh, darn it!

00:12:15.880 --> 00:12:16.720
It just...

00:12:16.720 --> 00:12:19.210
I don't know... It just makes 
me feel frazzled!

00:12:19.210 --> 00:12:22.170
I don't understand it! I don't 
deal well with this stuff!

00:12:22.170 --> 00:12:23.120
Huh?

00:12:23.120 --> 00:12:25.590
You said that earlier. 
What does "frazzled" mean?

00:12:25.590 --> 00:12:27.350
Frazzled means frazzled!

00:12:27.620 --> 00:12:28.500
Sana.

00:12:30.790 --> 00:12:32.670
Lately, I always feel this way.

00:12:33.240 --> 00:12:34.530
Even when I read books.

00:12:34.530 --> 00:12:37.890
And the moment I saw you 
two earlier, I felt frazzled.

00:12:37.890 --> 00:12:40.060
That's never happened before.

00:12:40.540 --> 00:12:42.050
What is this? What is it?

00:12:42.050 --> 00:12:44.370
I know I'm myself, 
but it's like I'm not!

00:12:44.370 --> 00:12:47.750
I never felt frazzled at 
the research facility.

00:12:47.750 --> 00:12:49.770
What is this? Tell me!

00:12:52.530 --> 00:12:55.860
S-Sa-chan, aren't you just angry

00:12:55.860 --> 00:12:58.000
that we ran from you?

00:12:58.930 --> 00:13:00.020
Uh...

00:13:00.020 --> 00:13:01.950
Yeah, I'm angry...

00:13:02.530 --> 00:13:03.340
Huh?

00:13:05.740 --> 00:13:07.250
Sana, sit down.

00:13:08.360 --> 00:13:09.130
Okay.

00:13:15.400 --> 00:13:18.860
Don't be shy, um...

00:13:19.130 --> 00:13:21.530
Oh, I am Hinagiri Yonaga.

00:13:21.530 --> 00:13:23.750
G-Go on, Onee-sama... You, too.

00:13:23.750 --> 00:13:25.490
Uh, I'm Asahi!

00:13:25.890 --> 00:13:28.080
Eat before it gets cold.

00:13:28.080 --> 00:13:28.950
Okay.

00:13:31.810 --> 00:13:33.910
U-Uh, then...

00:13:37.490 --> 00:13:38.660
This is good!

00:13:38.660 --> 00:13:39.540
It's very good!

00:13:39.930 --> 00:13:40.910
It's good, right?

00:13:40.910 --> 00:13:42.320
Yes, very!

00:13:42.320 --> 00:13:43.350
Yes!

00:13:52.140 --> 00:13:53.730
S-Sa-chan...

00:13:55.060 --> 00:13:58.780
Y-You... c-cut your hair, I see.

00:13:58.780 --> 00:14:00.040
Oh... Yeah.

00:14:00.040 --> 00:14:03.540
At first, I didn't recognize you.

00:14:03.540 --> 00:14:06.790
B-But I think it looks really good.

00:14:08.360 --> 00:14:09.900
It's an "up to you" bob!

00:14:09.900 --> 00:14:12.030
Wh-What's that? "Bob"?

00:14:12.030 --> 00:14:13.790
You don't know what a bob is?

00:14:13.010 --> 00:14:16.020
Those two were in the 
same place as Sana?

00:14:13.790 --> 00:14:14.730
It's a salon thing!

00:14:14.730 --> 00:14:17.330
Isn't it a barber shop thing?

00:14:16.480 --> 00:14:17.330
Yes.

00:14:19.240 --> 00:14:20.210
Errors?

00:14:20.210 --> 00:14:21.220
Yeah.

00:14:21.220 --> 00:14:25.020
Sometimes, my power just 
activates itself, like earlier.

00:14:25.630 --> 00:14:28.140
It doesn't always produce something.

00:14:28.140 --> 00:14:31.670
But when it does, I never know 
what it'll be, so it's dangerous.

00:14:31.670 --> 00:14:35.640
D-Don't you think you should 
have that checked out?

00:14:36.870 --> 00:14:39.730
Ichijo said she couldn't 
figure it out yet.

00:14:41.310 --> 00:14:43.250
H-Hey, Sa-chan...

00:14:44.450 --> 00:14:46.720
I'm s-sorry about earlier.

00:14:46.720 --> 00:14:49.740
The truth is, we've...

00:14:49.970 --> 00:14:52.650
We've really missed you, all this time!

00:14:53.320 --> 00:14:56.090
We wanted to apologize to you.

00:14:56.090 --> 00:14:57.620
Asahi? Yonaga?

00:14:58.480 --> 00:15:00.000
You know...

00:15:00.320 --> 00:15:03.750
Before we came to the research facility, 
something awful happened to us.

00:15:03.750 --> 00:15:07.460
That's why we didn't want you 
to go to the outside world.

00:15:07.460 --> 00:15:12.490
They were taken into police custody. 
Then the research facility took them in.

00:15:12.490 --> 00:15:13.760
Police?

00:15:13.760 --> 00:15:16.920
They'd been abused by their father.

00:15:35.310 --> 00:15:36.710
Get away...

00:15:37.310 --> 00:15:38.580
from her!

00:15:41.760 --> 00:15:45.170
At the time, they both thought 
and felt the same things,

00:15:45.170 --> 00:15:47.620
so they had trouble telling 
themselves apart.

00:15:48.310 --> 00:15:51.620
Starting today, this is your new home.

00:15:51.620 --> 00:15:53.380
Pretty big, isn't it?

00:15:53.380 --> 00:15:54.720
The air's nice, too.

00:15:55.200 --> 00:15:57.850
I can't let you go out 
whenever you want.

00:15:57.850 --> 00:16:00.830
But you can study, and you'll 
have a place to play.

00:16:00.830 --> 00:16:02.440
It isn't a bad place.

00:16:02.990 --> 00:16:06.660
What about your rooms? 
We can give you separate ones...

00:16:06.660 --> 00:16:08.290
We want a room together.

00:16:08.950 --> 00:16:09.890
Got it.

00:16:09.890 --> 00:16:11.670
You're in perfect sync, huh?

00:16:11.670 --> 00:16:13.450
Oh, right. Also...

00:16:13.670 --> 00:16:18.180
I'm sorry, but could you tell me 
your names one more time?

00:16:18.180 --> 00:16:20.950
These are your ID cards.

00:16:21.350 --> 00:16:24.300
Which of you is older, 
and which is younger?

00:16:28.490 --> 00:16:30.980
Then, I'm the older sister!

00:16:30.980 --> 00:16:36.070
I-I'm the younger sister, 
Hinagiri Yonaga...

00:16:37.750 --> 00:16:40.450
All we had to do was live together,

00:16:40.450 --> 00:16:43.890
just the two of us, and never 
leave the facility.

00:16:44.320 --> 00:16:45.850
That's what we thought.

00:16:46.070 --> 00:16:50.480
But then we met you and played 
with you, and it was fun.

00:16:50.880 --> 00:16:54.030
We gave you a name and taught 
you all kinds of things.

00:16:54.480 --> 00:16:59.540
But we never taught you that there was 
a world outside the research facility.

00:17:00.600 --> 00:17:02.640
We did a terrible thing to you.

00:17:03.000 --> 00:17:06.880
It wasn't as if you were our doll.

00:17:07.280 --> 00:17:12.060
But then you left on your own, 
and it changed our world.

00:17:12.460 --> 00:17:17.930
We never thought everything we 
had could disappear so easily.

00:17:32.190 --> 00:17:36.650
We're going to an American 
school in Yokosuka now.

00:17:37.020 --> 00:17:41.200
They found new homes for all of 
us from the research facility.

00:17:41.960 --> 00:17:45.280
Our place has a very nice dorm mother.

00:17:45.280 --> 00:17:47.610
The language is still a 
bit difficult for us,

00:17:47.610 --> 00:17:50.030
but slowly, we've begun 
to make friends, too.

00:17:50.030 --> 00:17:51.920
And we're even in clubs.

00:17:52.160 --> 00:17:55.600
I'm in the badminton club, 
and Onee-chan is in the art club.

00:17:55.600 --> 00:17:57.440
Is school fun?

00:17:58.230 --> 00:18:01.930
Well, yes... Every day is pretty fun.

00:18:01.930 --> 00:18:04.920
Really? Well, it's nice that it's fun.

00:18:05.480 --> 00:18:06.630
Sa-chan...

00:18:07.310 --> 00:18:10.310
We weren't able to spend 
much time with you,

00:18:10.310 --> 00:18:14.570
but you were our first friend, 
and that made us really happy.

00:18:15.040 --> 00:18:17.030
We're sorry, Sa-chan.

00:18:17.340 --> 00:18:19.540
We're sorry for everything!

00:18:21.420 --> 00:18:22.260
Sure!

00:18:24.140 --> 00:18:25.880
Okay, we've made up!

00:18:25.880 --> 00:18:27.490
Wait!

00:18:29.170 --> 00:18:33.750
Oh, really? And then what happened?

00:18:33.750 --> 00:18:37.010
Well, Asahi and Yonaga 
are both in clubs, too.

00:18:38.270 --> 00:18:41.010
Sana-chan, you just told me that.

00:18:41.010 --> 00:18:43.550
Huh? Oh, yeah.

00:18:43.550 --> 00:18:45.820
For some reason, I didn't think I had.

00:18:46.680 --> 00:18:48.460
You must've been really happy!

00:18:49.350 --> 00:18:50.710
I'm not sure.

00:18:50.710 --> 00:18:54.170
That sounds so nice... 
Your friends, huh?

00:19:14.410 --> 00:19:15.790
Sana-chan?

00:19:18.850 --> 00:19:20.210
Sanae!

00:19:20.210 --> 00:19:23.300
Huh? Sana-chan, come on!

00:19:24.190 --> 00:19:25.560
Are you all right?

00:19:25.560 --> 00:19:26.530
I was sleeping.

00:19:26.530 --> 00:19:29.070
And then suddenly, I didn't 
understand anything.

00:19:29.070 --> 00:19:30.340
I see.

00:19:30.750 --> 00:19:35.020
When I was little, I used to suddenly 
feel sad in the middle of the night.

00:19:35.020 --> 00:19:38.080
And I'd jump into Grandpa's futon.

00:19:38.080 --> 00:19:40.650
I'm not sad or anything.

00:19:41.060 --> 00:19:42.350
I think...

00:19:42.350 --> 00:19:44.000
Oh, yeah.

00:19:44.000 --> 00:19:47.390
You did have a really fun time earlier!

00:19:48.430 --> 00:19:49.650
It's weird...

00:19:50.060 --> 00:19:54.960
Ever since I left the research facility, 
I keep getting weirder.

00:19:54.960 --> 00:19:56.700
I feel frazzled.

00:19:57.140 --> 00:20:00.880
Like there's a frazzled person 
inside me that isn't me.

00:20:00.880 --> 00:20:04.010
And so, all the things I knew 
and thought before

00:20:04.010 --> 00:20:09.080
have become unclear, like the 
frazzled thing is interfering.

00:20:12.170 --> 00:20:13.560
It was the same today.

00:20:13.560 --> 00:20:16.310
The moment I saw them, I felt frazzled,

00:20:16.310 --> 00:20:18.510
and I couldn't think about anything.

00:20:18.980 --> 00:20:20.430
It's the same now.

00:20:20.430 --> 00:20:23.860
All of a sudden, I can't control myself.

00:20:24.360 --> 00:20:28.080
This keeps happening in the 
outside world. It's too hard.

00:20:28.080 --> 00:20:29.530
I see...

00:20:29.530 --> 00:20:33.960
You're starting to understand 
a lot of things, little by little.

00:20:34.170 --> 00:20:36.340
Huh? What are you talking about?

00:20:36.340 --> 00:20:38.770
I'm saying that I don't understand.

00:20:38.770 --> 00:20:40.690
Well, um...

00:20:40.690 --> 00:20:44.180
It's probably best that you don't 
understand, you might say...

00:20:44.440 --> 00:20:45.780
Huh?

00:20:46.460 --> 00:20:48.260
Frazzle, frazzle!

00:20:46.460 --> 00:20:50.270
What are you doing? Stop it!

00:20:52.000 --> 00:20:55.650
I love you a lot, Sana-chan.

00:20:55.650 --> 00:20:57.850
What's with you?! Are you teasing?

00:20:57.850 --> 00:21:01.200
I'm serious about feeling frazzled!

00:21:01.810 --> 00:21:04.610
Well, it's already late, so...

00:21:04.610 --> 00:21:07.350
Want to sleep in my room with me?

00:21:07.350 --> 00:21:08.370
Really?

00:21:08.600 --> 00:21:10.120
We can talk there.

00:21:10.120 --> 00:21:14.540
I want to hear more about 
how frazzled you feel!

00:21:25.350 --> 00:21:26.830
Morning, Yonaga.

00:21:26.830 --> 00:21:28.980
Good morning, Onee-sama.

00:21:30.920 --> 00:21:33.930
O-Onee-sama, we got an 
e-mail from Sa-chan!

00:21:33.930 --> 00:21:34.810
Huh?

00:21:35.320 --> 00:21:37.280
Isn't that great, Onee-sama?

00:21:37.280 --> 00:21:40.650
Y-You're the one who 
was worried about her!

00:21:40.650 --> 00:21:42.150
So were you.

00:21:43.810 --> 00:21:45.670
Did you send the e-mail?

00:21:45.670 --> 00:21:46.740
Yep.

00:21:46.960 --> 00:21:48.570
Do you still feel frazzled?

00:21:49.390 --> 00:21:50.580
I'm not sure.

00:21:51.030 --> 00:21:53.120
I think maybe not.

00:21:53.120 --> 00:21:54.340
Oh, good!

00:21:55.840 --> 00:21:57.740
<b>"Sorry I left the research facility.</b>

00:21:58.040 --> 00:22:00.230
<b>You two are my friends.</b>

00:22:01.270 --> 00:22:02.740
<b>Let's play together again.</b>

00:22:02.740 --> 00:22:04.240
<b>— Kashimura Sana."</b>

00:23:34.930 --> 00:23:39.930
Next Episode 
The Evil Witch

00:23:36.090 --> 00:23:37.450
The Evil Witch.
